{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"115624","commit":"5755968002086a78a66840628de4680f868407da","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The introduction of the `limit` field in `MvExpand` and its handling in `writeTo`, `hashCode`, and `equals` methods is correct. However, there should be logic to set this `limit` value when creating an instance of `MvExpand`. Ensure that constructors or factory methods are updated to accept and store the `limit` value.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java--3936:3941","promptId":"#KFPW9","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":3936,"endPos":3941,"startLine":127,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":127,"endLineOffset":69,"length":6}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java--2312:2333","promptId":"#ZQ1R4","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":2312,"endPos":2333,"startLine":61,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":61,"endLineOffset":29,"length":22}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java-3718:3741,3761:3796-4091:4125,4164:4176,4181:4221,4240:4258","promptId":"#S1M8H","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":3718,"endPos":3741,"startLine":123,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":123,"endLineOffset":61,"length":24},{"pos":3761,"endPos":3796,"startLine":123,"startLineOffset":81,"endLine":123,"endLineOffset":116,"length":36}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":4091,"endPos":4125,"startLine":135,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":135,"endLineOffset":42,"length":35},{"pos":4164,"endPos":4176,"startLine":136,"startLineOffset":38,"endLine":136,"endLineOffset":50,"length":13},{"pos":4181,"endPos":4221,"startLine":136,"startLineOffset":55,"endLine":136,"endLineOffset":95,"length":41},{"pos":4240,"endPos":4258,"startLine":136,"startLineOffset":114,"endLine":136,"endLineOffset":132,"length":19}]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java--1229:1257","promptId":"#FQG9M","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/plan/logical/MvExpand.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1229,"endPos":1257,"startLine":30,"startLineOffset":4,"endLine":30,"endLineOffset":32,"length":29}]}]},{"comment":"The addition of a new capability flag `ADD_LIMIT_INSIDE_MV_EXPAND` is not accompanied by any logic that utilizes this flag or modifies behavior based on it. Ensure that there are corresponding changes elsewhere to handle this new capability.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/action/EsqlCapabilities.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/action/EsqlCapabilities.java--13516:13614","promptId":"#HVQGD","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/action/EsqlCapabilities.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/action/EsqlCapabilities.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":13516,"endPos":13614,"startLine":446,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":449,"endLineOffset":34,"length":99}]}]},{"comment":"The assumption that `limitSource.fold()` will always return an integer is made without explicit checks or documentation. Ensure that `fold()` on the limit expression always returns an integer in this context.\nThe condition `mvxLimit \u003d\u003d null || mvxLimit \u003c 0 || mvxLimit \u003e limitVal` should be well-documented to explain why these specific conditions are checked and what they represent.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/PushDownAndCombineLimits.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/PushDownAndCombineLimits.java-1859:1934,1947:2007,2020:2087,2105:2535-1852:3531","promptId":"#9T1V4","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/PushDownAndCombineLimits.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/PushDownAndCombineLimits.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1859,"endPos":1934,"startLine":37,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":37,"endLineOffset":87,"length":76},{"pos":1947,"endPos":2007,"startLine":38,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":38,"endLineOffset":72,"length":61},{"pos":2020,"endPos":2087,"startLine":39,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":39,"endLineOffset":79,"length":68},{"pos":2105,"endPos":2535,"startLine":40,"startLineOffset":17,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":13,"length":431}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1852,"endPos":3531,"startLine":36,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":64,"endLineOffset":13,"length":1680}]}]},{"comment":"The removal of `DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand` from the optimizer rules list in `LogicalPlanOptimizer#operators` and its subsequent handling in `Mapper#map` suggest that the logic for managing limits after `MvExpand` operations has been refactored. However, this change introduces a potential issue: the rule `DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand` was designed to ensure that limits are appropriately managed before and after `MvExpand` operations, especially in cases where there might be multiple limits or when the order of operations could affect performance or correctness.\nBy removing `DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand`, you are assuming that all necessary limit management is now handled within the `Mapper#map` method. This assumption should be validated to ensure that no scenarios previously covered by `DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand` are now being overlooked. Specifically, consider the following:\n1. **Multiple Limits**: Ensure that if there are multiple limits in a query plan, they are correctly managed and not inadvertently overridden or ignored.\n2. **Order of Operations**: Verify that the order of operations (e.g., sorting, filtering) does not affect the correctness of limit application after `MvExpand`.\n3. **Performance Considerations**: Ensure that pushing down limits where possible still results in optimal query performance.\nTo mitigate these risks, it is recommended to:\n- Review and test scenarios involving multiple limits and complex query plans.\n- Ensure that the logic in `Mapper#map` covers all cases previously handled by `DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand`.\n- Add or update test cases to cover these scenarios.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand.java--0:252,1101:5266-","promptId":"#MRA3E","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/rules/logical/DuplicateLimitAfterMvExpand.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":0,"endPos":252,"startLine":1,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":6,"endLineOffset":3,"length":253},{"pos":1101,"endPos":5266,"startLine":24,"startLineOffset":0,"endLine":108,"endLineOffset":1,"length":4166}],"dstChanges":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java-10015:10048-","promptId":"#9JB45","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizer.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10015,"endPos":10048,"startLine":177,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":177,"endLineOffset":45,"length":34}],"dstChanges":[]},{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/planner/Mapper.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/planner/Mapper.java-10474:10572-10638:10759,10772:11075,11095:11101","promptId":"#RWZPP","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/planner/Mapper.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/planner/Mapper.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":10474,"endPos":10572,"startLine":231,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":231,"endLineOffset":117,"length":99}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":10638,"endPos":10759,"startLine":234,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":234,"endLineOffset":133,"length":122},{"pos":10772,"endPos":11075,"startLine":235,"startLineOffset":12,"endLine":239,"endLineOffset":13,"length":304},{"pos":11095,"endPos":11101,"startLine":240,"startLineOffset":19,"endLine":240,"endLineOffset":25,"length":7}]}]},{"comment":"In the test `testMultiMvExpand_SortDownBelow`, there is another TODO comment about double-checking the `AddDefaultTopN` rule. Similar to the previous point, ensure that this rule is correctly implemented and verified to match the expected behavior.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java-x-pack/plugin/esql/src/test/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/optimizer/LogicalPlanOptimizerTests.java--61947:63446,63452:64346,64352:65471,65477:66619,66625:67491","promptId":"#7JTFF","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/